needle='## Requirement and acceptance traceability\n'
addition='''## Source projection, capture epoch and storage contract

The executable producer now retains all versioned SDK-index records, including historical/future entries. A native current-target flag is used only for current annotation/JVM-equivalence lookup; it is never a claim about a running device or installed SDK extensions. The catalog projection keeps immutable source declarations intact while enriching derived registry entries with proven same-snapshot TypeReference IDs and versioned inventory variants. Each variant uses the shared dispatch contract digest and pins its containing/argument/return/structured-field type schemas. SDK lifecycle ranges and declared extension alternatives are source-backed; a standalone occurrence labeled37.2 proves that minor point, not every37.x release. Unknown or ambiguous types/lifetimes remain visible, and a proven version exclusion remains unavailable even when another schema fact is unknown. The complete registry_inventory is exported with a versioned manifest and independently reconciled against Entry hashes, source evidence, type hashes and stream bytes; absent or partial legacy inventories cannot initialize a startup view.

Facts are captured with capability_epoch and observed_at. The resolver rejects epoch relabeling; publication also verifies the exact facts hash, scope and current epoch. A non-authoritative positive module/interface observation remains unknown. Malformed intervals are quarantined with APPLICABILITY_MALFORMED without discarding unrelated inventory. Every available root/type graph has graph_digest over the sorted transitive root/type(entry_id,schema_hash) closure; publication recomputes it. This is schema identity, not proof of a Binder codec or permission.

DeviceResolution2.0.0 supersedes the unimplemented1.2draft because epoch-bound facts and graph digests are now required. Older draft snapshots remain historical and cannot be activated silently. Entry1.1 and catalog storage1.2 remain separate contracts; OpenAPI specification version is1.3.0. Offline generated aliases can consume the fresh trusted-store view and use exactly the selected generic schema and graph digest; the complete inventory remains discoverable. They remain default-deny and unavailable for execution until live authority and verified wire/codec contracts pass the shared admission gate.

The executable configuration DDL stores immutable facts, staged/sealed device_views and device_view_entries, a scoped generation/epoch/catalog/overlay CAS pointer and append-only invalidation reasons. A catalog-pinned expected_inventory_count and coherent dependency check reject partial activation. SQLite JSON/normalized columns agree; active/pinned snapshots cannot be collected. binding_availability is a read-only fresh projection, not an independent cache authority. Versioned binding_wire_contracts stores interface version/hash, transaction code, flags/oneway and codec/proof evidence separately from existence. device_view_storage is an offline transaction reference; Android collectors, Binder execution, HTTP/MCP service deployment and actual OS permission grants remain runtime integration gates.

'''
assert needle in s and '## Source projection, capture epoch and storage contract' not in s;s=s.replace(needle,addition+needle)
